# Godot
.godot/
godot/.godot/
*.import
# ...except the art's. An .import file holds a picture's import settings and
# the uid other files can name it by, and Godot's documentation says to commit
# it. The imported copy itself lives under .godot/ and stays out.
!godot/assets/**/*.import
# export_presets.cfg is committed (T24): `make export` needs the preset, and
# since Godot 4.1 the secrets an export may carry live in
# .godot/export_credentials.cfg, which the line above already keeps out.

# Build and release output
dist/
build/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Generated model weights live in dist/, never committed from a local run.
# The checked-in weights.json under godot/addons/ai_learning/ is produced by
# `make train` and committed deliberately, so it is NOT ignored here.

# gdUnit4 writes HTML/XML reports next to the project on every run.
godot/reports/

# gdUnit4 is installed by `make bootstrap`, not vendored. 509 files of someone
# else's code would dominate the history of a repository whose point is that
# you can read it. See docs/adr/0004.
godot/addons/gdUnit4/

# The forbidden-term list is deliberately NOT in the repository. A review
# brute-forced a short term from the published salt and length in 0.02s, so a
# committed hash file is the employer's name in the repository -- the thing
# invariant 10 forbids. It lives only on the author's machine now, built by
# `python3 scripts/check_no_employer_refs.py --add-term`. See docs/adr/0005.
scripts/forbidden-term-hashes.txt

# Reviewer worktrees made by the coding assistant: never part of the repo.
.claude/worktrees/

# A person's own generated art (T31). Theirs, never the repository's: the game
# draws from here when a picture is present and falls back on the CC0 set.
godot/assets/generated/
